+/* Metric-matched fallbacks.
+   Both webfonts load from Google, and until they arrive the browser draws the
+   page in a system face of a different width. When the real face swaps in,
+   headings re-wrap and everything below them jumps: measured at CLS 0.366 on
+   the country pages, against Google's 0.1 threshold, with an h1 changing height
+   by 65px as it went from two lines to one.
+
+   These faces are Arial re-proportioned to occupy the same space as the real
+   ones, so the swap changes the shapes without moving the layout. The numbers
+   are measured, not estimated: the sample string is rendered in each real face
+   and in Arial at the same size, and the ratio of the two widths is the
+   size-adjust. The ascent and descent overrides are expressed against that
+   already-adjusted em, which is why they are divided by the same ratio.
+   Re-measure with agent-lead-fontmetrics.mjs if either family ever changes. */
+@font-face {
+  font-family: "Space Grotesk Fallback";
+  src: local("Arial");
+  size-adjust: 101.4%;
+  ascent-override: 96.6%;
+  descent-override: 28.6%;
+  line-gap-override: 0%;
+}
+@font-face {
